      "writtenOn": "2024-01-24T17:48:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Note that there\u0027s a third option: use `dtc` to dump `/sys/firmware/device-tree` as a DTB (\"`-I fs -O dtb`\", IIRC), which can then be parsed by our `libfdt` wrappers. A bit convoluted but would involve less code than writing (and having to test, maintain, ...) `fs_to_fdt`.\n\nYou might want to check if we can even call directly into the DTC code doing the \"DT dumping\" so that we don\u0027t need to manage a separate binary?\n\n(assuming DTC and libfdt have the same license but I vaguely remember they might not, so that should also be checked)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 16,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 16,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "381a8a4995005b443456a37b8c9b3161b44d19c7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
